  "description": "alarms.v1 §2.2, §2.3, §2.12. Each case has an `op`. `derive`: a rule and its labels (a JSON object of strings, host-scoped labels included) -> `key`, the alert key a reader derives through the sanitizing step (§2.3), `input`, the string hashed (its UTF-8 bytes), and `framed`, whether the strict recipe (§2.2) accepts the rule and labels as they are; on framed input the two recipes give one key. `host_scoped`: a label name -> whether it is host-scoped (§2.2), compared exactly. `ref`: a reference's system, service and alert key -> the alarm's key (§2.12), the alert key slugged (core §1.4), or null when the system or the service is no name (core §1.2). `parse`: a key -> the reference it names, the alert key unslugged, or null when it is not a key of alarms.v1's one template."
